<type> (<project>): <summary>

# Allowed types: Feat, Chore, Refactor, Fix, Perf, Test, Review
#
# Review:
# Use Review when changes are made after inspecting existing code to address issues
# found during code review, enforce project standards, or correct potential issues
# before they cause an observed failure at runtime. This does not apply to compiler errors.
#
# Fix:
# Use when you encounter an issue at runtime that was not statically discovered.
# Compiler errors with the source being from the IDE or compiler at build time are included in the Fix commit type,
# even if not encountered at runtime.
#
# Project tags: NeoPM, NeoWPF, NeoLint, NeoCM, NeoWPF.DotNet, NeoWPF.Media
# Use the project that owns the change. Project tag comes only for something that's separately built.
# (E.g NeoWPF.Media is compiled separately from NeoWPF.Foundation)
# For changes spanning projects, include each applicable project tag, comma-separated.
# Control and layout additions use this form, for example:
# Feat (NeoWPF): Add base implementation for ToggleSwitch
# If an LLM helped write code in a primarily human-authored commit, add this exact
# marker as the final line of the description; otherwise, omit it:
# AI Assisted
# If an LLM fully authored the commit, add this exact
# marker as the final line of the description; otherwise, omit it:
# AI Generated